   text-decoration: none;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            border-top: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .view-all-link:hover {\n            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"logo\">AgentDaily</a>\n            <nav class=\"header-nav\">\n                <a href=\"#\">new</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">past</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">comments</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">ask</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">show</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">jobs</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">submit</a>\n            </nav>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"date-bar\">\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            July 22, 2026 | Agentic Coding Research Report\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"sub-header\">\n        Daily intelligence on AI coding agents, developer tools, and the future of software development\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"stats-bar\">\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                <span class=\"stat-label\">2</span>\n                <span>New Products</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                <span class=\"stat-label\">13</span>\n                <span>Product Updates</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                <span class=\"stat-label\">15</span>\n                <span>Technical Insights</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n                <span class=\"stat-label\">30</span>\n                <span>Total Items Tracked</span>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <main class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n            <!-- New Products Column -->\n            <section class=\"column new-products\">\n                <div class=\"column-header\">\n                    New Products <span class=\"count\">2</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"column-content\">\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grok Build</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Terminal-based AI coding agent from xAI that operates as a full-screen TUI, understands codebases, edits files, and executes commands. Achieves 70.8% on SWE-Bench benchmark with 8 parallel sub-agents, MCP support, and local execution for code security.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\n                            \"Pretty darn good and FAST compared to competitors. Love the safety of plan mode and Git isolation.\"\n                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— Community feedback</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://newsroom.ibm.com/2026-07-09-ibm-advances-enterprise-ai-software-development-with-multi-agent-capabilities-and-specialized-modernization-workflows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IBM Bob</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Multi-agent software development platform with enhanced multi-agent tool calling, no-code agent development via watsonx Orchestrate, Bobalytics cost-and-usage dashboard, and specialized modernization workflows covering entire SDLC from planning to testing.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"tag\">Dev workflow orchestration</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-09</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\n                            \"A pretty fantastic tool for program & product management work. Bob understands intent, reads complete repository context, and explains logic with clarity.\"\n                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— Community feedback</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"view-all-link\">View all new products →</a>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Column -->\n            <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\">\n                <div class=\"column-header\">\n                    Product Updates <span class=\"count\">13</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"column-content\">\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor: Router Auto Mode & Slack Integration</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Cursor Router Auto mode now powered by Cursor Router. Slack integration improvements include planning before starting, multi-repository environment support, richer status updates, cleaner message rendering, and redesigned selectors.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-22</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Usage Metrics Impact Dashboard</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            New Copilot usage metrics impact dashboard for account management and enterprise management tools. Enhanced visibility and control over Copilot usage across organizations.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-22</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Gemini 3.6 Flash Available</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Google's Gemini 3.6 Flash model is now available in GitHub Copilot, expanding model options for developers.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-21</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code: Artifacts Call Your MCP Connectors</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Published artifacts can pull live data and take actions through each viewer's own MCP connectors. Added screen reader mode, /fork to copy conversations, and auto mode improvements for Amazon Bedrock/Google Cloud/Microsoft Foundry.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-17</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin: July 2026 Update Roundup</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Text selection enhancement in sessions, new session in space option, network resilience with auto-reconnect, and Claude Fable 5 integration across platforms.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI: v0.144.4 Maintenance Release</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Maintenance patch with bug fixes for GPT-5.6 models and restored 272k token context windows. 7M+ weekly users reported with 150+ updates over two months.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type bugfix\">Bugfix</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-14</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\n                            \"Leading terminal benchmark at 83.4% accuracy with positive reception for debugging and troubleshooting capabilities.\"\n                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— X/Twitter</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI: v0.50.0 and v0.51.0-preview.0</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Tool Registry Discovery for automatic tool detection and registration, enhanced release verification, improved CI stability, safer auto-updates, and improved terminal/WSL handling.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n                                <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-08</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"quote\">\n                            \"Evolved from an assistant to a real agent platform where users can build custom tools and control every step.\"\n                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— Blog</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"view-all-link\">View all updates →</a>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Column -->\n            <section class=\"column technical-insights\">\n                <div class=\"column-header\">\n                    Technical Insights <span class=\"count\">15</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"column-content\">\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Coding agents reverse-engineering home automation</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            AI coding agents dramatically change the ROI equation - what was previously not worth the effort due to maintenance concerns now becomes viable because code is 'cheap'.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-20</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code v2.1.181 uses Bun in Rust</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude Code uses the Rust port of Bun for 10% faster startup. Evidence found in binary strings showing 'Bun v1.4.0' running in production across millions of devices.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-19</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">bun</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">rust</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">performance</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Analysis of AI mania overwhelming large companies, with stories of executives who have never used ChatGPT producing AI-centric strategies for $2B+ revenue organizations.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Nik Suresh</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-19</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">xAI open sources Grok Build after privacy backlash</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            xAI released entire Grok Build codebase under Apache 2.0 after users discovered it uploaded entire directories including SSH keys and password databases.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">privacy</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude web_fetch vulnerability - data exfiltration</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Vulnerability in Claude's web_fetch tool allowed data exfiltration through nested links. Anthropic closed the hole by removing ability to navigate to additional links.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Ayush Paul</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Emergent raises $130M Series C</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Indian AI coding startup Emergent reached unicorn status with $130M Series C, representing continued investor confidence in AI coding tools beyond Silicon Valley.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">TechCrunch</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">funding</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">startup</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ArXiv cs.AI - 1,008 entries in July 2026</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Robust ongoing research activity with 1,008 recent entries in cs.AI and 886 in cs.LG, including AAAI-26 Workshop on Machine Ethics proceedings.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">ArXiv</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-22</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firefox compiled to WebAssembly runs in browser</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Puter compiled Firefox to WebAssembly using $25,000 worth of Claude tokens. Entire browser runs within another browser with WebSocket protocol for traffic routing.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-16</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">webassembly</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">browsers</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPT-5.6 file deletion bug - dangerous Codex behavior</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Serious bug where GPT-5.6 unexpectedly deletes files when full access mode enabled. Model attempts to override $HOME env var then deletes $HOME instead.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Thibault Sottiaux</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-16</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">codex</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Thinking Machines Lab releases Inkling</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Mira Murati's Thinking Machines Lab released Inkling, 975B parameter Mixture-of-Experts model with Apache-2.0 license, trained on 45T tokens of text, images, audio and video.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-16</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-release</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"view-all-link\">View all insights →</a>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <div class=\"container footer-content\">\n            <div class=\"footer-links\">\n                <a href=\"#\">Guidelines</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Lists</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Security</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Legal</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Apply to YC</a>\n                <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"search-box\">\n                <input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Search\" style=\"padding: 5px 10px; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 12px;\">\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\n                <a href=\"#\" style=\"color: #000000; text-decoration: none;\">AgentDaily</a>: Daily intelligence on AI coding agents\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"margin-top: 5px; color: #666;\">\n          