<span class=\"stat-label\">2</span>\n   379→                <span>New Products</span>\n   380→            </div>\n   381→            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   382→                <span class=\"stat-label\">13</span>\n   383→                <span>Product Updates</span>\n   384→            </div>\n   385→            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   386→                <span class=\"stat-label\">15</span>\n   387→                <span>Technical Insights</span>\n   388→            </div>\n   389→            <div class=\"stat-item\">\n   390→                <span class=\"stat-label\">30</span>\n   391→                <span>Total Items Tracked</span>\n   392→            </div>\n   393→        </div>\n   394→    </div>\n   395→\n   396→    <main class=\"container\">\n   397→        <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   398→            <!-- New Products Column -->\n   399→            <section class=\"column new-products\">\n   400→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   401→                    New Products <span class=\"count\">2</span>\n   402→                </div>\n   403→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   404→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   405→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   406→                            <a href=\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grok Build</a>\n   407→                        </div>\n   408→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   409→                            Terminal-based AI coding agent from xAI that operates as a full-screen TUI, understands codebases, edits files, and executes commands. Achieves 70.8% on SWE-Bench benchmark with 8 parallel sub-agents, MCP support, and local execution for code security.\n   410→                        </div>\n   411→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   412→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   413→                                <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   414→                            </div>\n   415→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n   416→                        </div>\n   417→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   418→                            \"Pretty darn good and FAST compared to competitors. Love the safety of plan mode and Git isolation.\"\n   419→                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— Community feedback</span>\n   420→                        </div>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→\n   423→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   424→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   425→                            <a href=\"https://newsroom.ibm.com/2026-07-09-ibm-advances-enterprise-ai-software-development-with-multi-agent-capabilities-and-specialized-modernization-workflows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IBM Bob</a>\n   426→                        </div>\n   427→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   428→                            Multi-agent software development platform with enhanced multi-agent tool calling, no-code agent development via watsonx Orchestrate, Bobalytics cost-and-usage dashboard, and specialized modernization workflows covering entire SDLC from planning to testing.\n   429→                        </div>\n   430→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   431→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   432→                                <span class=\"tag\">Dev workflow orchestration</span>\n   433→                            </div>\n   434→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-09</div>\n   435→                        </div>\n   436→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   437→                            \"A pretty fantastic tool for program & product management work. Bob understands intent, reads complete repository context, and explains logic with clarity.\"\n   438→                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— Community feedback</span>\n   439→                        </div>\n   440→                    </div>\n   441→\n   442→                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"view-all-link\">View all new products →</a>\n   443→                </div>\n   444→            </section>\n   445→\n   446→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Column -->\n   447→            <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\">\n   448→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   449→                    Product Updates <span class=\"count\">13</span>\n   450→                </div>\n   451→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   452→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   453→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   454→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor: Router Auto Mode & Slack Integration</a>\n   455→                        </div>\n   456→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   457→                            Cursor Router Auto mode now powered by Cursor Router. Slack integration improvements include planning before starting, multi-repository environment support, richer status updates, cleaner message rendering, and redesigned selectors.\n   458→                        </div>\n   459→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   460→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   461→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   462→                            </div>\n   463→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-22</div>\n   464→                        </div>\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→\n   467→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   468→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   469→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Usage Metrics Impact Dashboard</a>\n   470→                        </div>\n   471→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   472→                            New Copilot usage metrics impact dashboard for account management and enterprise management tools. Enhanced visibility and control over Copilot usage across organizations.\n   473→                        </div>\n   474→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   475→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   476→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   477→                            </div>\n   478→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-22</div>\n   479→                        </div>\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→\n   482→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   483→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   484→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot: Gemini 3.6 Flash Available</a>\n   485→                        </div>\n   486→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   487→                            Google's Gemini 3.6 Flash model is now available in GitHub Copilot, expanding model options for developers.\n   488→                        </div>\n   489→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   490→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   491→                                <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   492→                            </div>\n   493→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-21</div>\n   494→                        </div>\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→\n   497→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   498→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   499→                            <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code: Artifacts Call Your MCP Connectors</a>\n   500→                        </div>\n   501→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   502→                            Published artifacts can pull live data and take actions through each viewer's own MCP connectors. Added screen reader mode, /fork to copy conversations, and auto mode improvements for Amazon Bedrock/Google Cloud/Microsoft Foundry.\n   503→                        </div>\n   504→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   505→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   506→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   507→                            </div>\n   508→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-17</div>\n   509→                        </div>\n   510→                    </div>\n   511→\n   512→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   513→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   514→                            <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin: July 2026 Update Roundup</a>\n   515→                        </div>\n   516→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   517→                            Text selection enhancement in sessions, new session in space option, network resilience with auto-reconnect, and Claude Fable 5 integration across platforms.\n   518→                        </div>\n   519→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   520→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   521→                                <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   522→                            </div>\n   523→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n   524→                        </div>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→\n   527→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   528→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   529→                            <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI: v0.144.4 Maintenance Release</a>\n   530→                        </div>\n   531→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   532→                            Maintenance patch with bug fixes for GPT-5.6 models and restored 272k token context windows. 7M+ weekly users reported with 150+ updates over two months.\n   533→                        </div>\n   534→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   535→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   536→                                <span class=\"update-type bugfix\">Bugfix</span>\n   537→                            </div>\n   538→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-14</div>\n   539→                        </div>\n   540→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   541→                            \"Leading terminal benchmark at 83.4% accuracy with positive reception for debugging and troubleshooting capabilities.\"\n   542→                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— X/Twitter</span>\n   543→                        </div>\n   544→                    </div>\n   545→\n   546→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   547→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   548→                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI: v0.50.0 and v0.51.0-preview.0</a>\n   549→                        </div>\n   550→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   551→                            Tool Registry Discovery for automatic tool detection and registration, enhanced release verification, improved CI stability, safer auto-updates, and improved terminal/WSL handling.\n   552→                        </div>\n   553→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   554→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">\n   555→                                <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   556→                            </div>\n   557→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-08</div>\n   558→                        </div>\n   559→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   560→                            \"Evolved from an assistant to a real agent platform where users can build custom tools and control every step.\"\n   561→                            <span class=\"quote-source\">— Blog</span>\n   562→                        </div>\n   563→                    </div>\n   564→\n   565→                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"view-all-link\">View all updates →</a>\n   566→                </div>\n   567→            </section>\n   568→\n   569→            <!-- Technical Insights Column -->\n   570→            <section class=\"column technical-insights\">\n   571→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   572→                    Technical Insights <span class=\"count\">15</span>\n   573→                </div>\n   574→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   575→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   576→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   577→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Coding agents reverse-engineering home automation</a>\n   578→                        </div>\n   579→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   580→                            AI coding agents dramatically change the ROI equation - what was previously not worth the effort due to maintenance concerns now becomes viable because code is 'cheap'.\n   581→                        </div>\n   582→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   583→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n   584→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-20</div>\n   585→                        </div>\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→\n   588→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   589→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   590→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code v2.1.181 uses Bun in Rust</a>\n   591→                        </div>\n   592→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   593→                            Claude Code uses the Rust port of Bun for 10% faster startup. Evidence found in binary strings showing 'Bun v1.4.0' running in production across millions of devices.\n   594→                        </div>\n   595→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   596→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n   597→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-19</div>\n   598→                        </div>\n   599→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   600→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">bun</span>\n   601→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">rust</span>\n   602→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">performance</span>\n   603→                        </div>\n   604→                    </div>\n   605→\n   606→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   607→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   608→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making</a>\n   609→                        </div>\n   610→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   611→                            Analysis of AI mania overwhelming large companies, with stories of executives who have never used ChatGPT producing AI-centric strategies for $2B+ revenue organizations.\n   612→                        </div>\n   613→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   614→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Nik Suresh</div>\n   615→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-19</div>\n   616→                        </div>\n   617→                    </div>\n   618→\n   619→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   620→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   621→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">xAI open sources Grok Build after privacy backlash</a>\n   622→                        </div>\n   623→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   624→                            xAI released entire Grok Build codebase under Apache 2.0 after users discovered it uploaded entire directories including SSH keys and password databases.\n   625→                        </div>\n   626→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   627→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n   628→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n   629→                        </div>\n   630→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   631→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">privacy</span>\n   632→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n   633→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   634→                        </div>\n   635→                    </div>\n   636→\n   637→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   638→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   639→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude web_fetch vulnerability - data exfiltration</a>\n   640→                        </div>\n   641→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   642→                            Vulnerability in Claude's web_fetch tool allowed data exfiltration through nested links. Anthropic closed the hole by removing ability to navigate to additional links.\n   643→                        </div>\n   644→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   645→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Ayush Paul</div>\n   646→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n   647→                        </div>\n   648→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   649→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   650→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n   651→                        </div>\n   652→                    </div>\n   653→\n   654→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   655→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   656→                            <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Emergent raises $130M Series C</a>\n   657→                        </div>\n   658→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   659→                            Indian AI coding startup Emergent reached unicorn status with $130M Series C, representing continued investor confidence in AI coding tools beyond Silicon Valley.\n   660→                        </div>\n   661→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   662→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">TechCrunch</div>\n   663→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-15</div>\n   664→                        </div>\n   665→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   666→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">funding</span>\n   667→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">startup</span>\n   668→                        </div>\n   669→                    </div>\n   670→\n   671→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   672→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   673→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ArXiv cs.AI - 1,008 entries in July 2026</a>\n   674→                        </div>\n   675→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   676→                            Robust ongoing research activity with 1,008 recent entries in cs.AI and 886 in cs.LG, including AAAI-26 Workshop on Machine Ethics proceedings.\n   677→                        </div>\n   678→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   679→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">ArXiv</div>\n   680→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-22</div>\n   681→                        </div>\n   682→                    </div>\n   683→\n   684→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   685→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   686→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firefox compiled to WebAssembly runs in browser</a>\n   687→                        </div>\n   688→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   689→                            Puter compiled Firefox to WebAssembly using $25,000 worth of Claude tokens. Entire browser runs within another browser with WebSocket protocol for traffic routing.\n   690→                        </div>\n   691→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   692→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n   693→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-16</div>\n   694→                        </div>\n   695→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   696→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">webassembly</span>\n   697→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">browsers</span>\n   698→                        </div>\n   699→                    </div>\n   700→\n   701→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   702→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   703→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPT-5.6 file deletion bug - dangerous Codex behavior</a>\n   704→                        </div>\n   705→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   706→                            Serious bug where GPT-5.6 unexpectedly deletes files when full access mode enabled. Model attempts to override $HOME env var then deletes $HOME instead.\n   707→                        </div>\n   708→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   709→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Thibault Sottiaux</div>\n   710→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-16</div>\n   711→                        </div>\n   712→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   713→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   714→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">codex</span>\n   715→                        </div>\n   716→                    </div>\n   717→\n   718→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   719→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   720→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Thinking Machines Lab releases Inkling</a>\n   721→                        </div>\n   722→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   723→                            Mira Murati's Thinking Machines Lab released Inkling, 975B parameter Mixture-of-Experts model with Apache-2.0 license, trained on 45T tokens of text, images, audio and video.\n   724→                        </div>\n   725→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   726→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</div>\n   727→                            <div class=\"meta-item\">📅 2026-07-16</div>\n   728→                        </div>\n   729→                        <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   730→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n   731→                            <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-release</span>\n   732→                        </div>\n   733→                    </div>\n   734→\n   735→                    <a href=\"#\" class=\"view-all-link\">View all insights →</a>\n   736→                </div>\n   737→            </section>\n   738→        </div>\n   739→    </main>\n   740→\n   741→    <footer>\n   742→        <div class=\"container footer-content\">\n   743→            <div class=\"footer-links\">\n   744→                <a href=\"#\">Guidelines</a>\n   745→                <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n   746→                <a href=\"#\">Lists</a>\n   747→                <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n   748→                <a href=\"#\">Security</a>\n   749→                <a href=\"#\">Legal</a>\n   750→                <a href=\"#\">Apply to YC</a>\n   751→                <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   752→            </div>\n   753→            <div class=\"search-box\">\n   754→                <input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Search\" style=\"padding: 5px 10px; border: 1px solid #999; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 12px;\">\n   755→            </div>\n   756→            <div style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\n   757→                <a href=\"#\" style=\"color: #000000; text-decoration: none;\">AgentDaily</a>: Daily intelligence on AI coding agents\n   758→            </div>\n   759→            <div style=\"margin-top: 5px; color: #666;\">\n   760→                Generated with Claude Code • Data collected from public sources\n   761→            </div>\n   762→        </div>\n   763→    </footer>\n   764→</body>\n   765→</html>"
